  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.1.0: first release. AddLineLogin() on AuthenticationBuilder registers a LINE Login scheme over the first-party OAuthHandler: PKCE on by default, a nonce carried through the OAuth state and checked against the id_token, bot_prompt for the add-friend flow, profile claims (NameIdentifier, Name, picture, status message), an optional friendship claim, and local HS256 validation of the id_token that fails the whole sign-in when it does not verify. PublicOrigin pins redirect_uri to a stated public address at both the authorisation step and the token exchange, which is what a reverse proxy without X-Forwarded-Proto otherwise gets wrong. MapLineWebhook() maps an endpoint that verifies X-Line-Signature before parsing, answers 401 on a bad signature and 400 on an unparsable body, isolates each event's handler so one failure does not stop the batch, and can run keyword auto reply before the handler with the outcome left in HttpContext.Items. See https://github.com/ozakboy/Ozakboy.Line/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
